    meaning: "The Court card represents legal and official matters of all kinds. This includes actual courtroom proceedings, contracts, official documents, disputes that require third-party resolution, and any situation where a formal judgment is rendered. The card speaks of justice, both legal and karmic. The outcome of the court matter is indicated by the cards around it. With the Good Gentleman (5) or Good Lady (6), a favorable outcome with wise counsel. With False Person (8), deceit in legal matters or an unjust verdict. With Sad News (14), a negative outcome. The Court card can also represent an internal judgment: the querent's own conscience or their sense of right and wrong. In a non-legal reading, the card indicates that a decision must be made and that the querent's choice will have consequences. The card asks the querent to act with integrity and to trust that fair outcomes will prevail. When the Court card appears, it is time to seek clarity and resolution through proper channels.",
